course: dictionary
lesson: 12609
title: Discourtesy: rude, but in a formal way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Discourtesy is a formal word for rude, impolite behaviour that shows a lack of respect for other people. «It would be a discourtesy to arrive late.» The sentence tells you the arriving late was impolite, even though it does not say the word rude.
explain: Look at the word's parts for a clue. Courtesy means good manners, and dis- means not, so discourtesy is the opposite of good manners. You can also swap in an easier word to check: «It would be rude to arrive late» still makes sense.
explain: Writers use discourtesy in letters, school reports and old stories, where a careful, grown-up voice is wanted. «Her discourtesy to the visitor was noted in the report.» The formal tone is part of the clue: this is serious, not a joke.
fact: Discourtesy means rude, impolite behaviour that shows a lack of respect.
fact: A discourtesy is one rude act, such as ignoring someone or not saying thank you.
fact: Discourtesy is a formal word, so you will often find it in letters, school reports and old stories.
fact: «Discourteous» is the adjective: «a discourteous reply» is a rude reply.
fact: Courtesy means polite behaviour, and the prefix dis- means not, so discourtesy is its opposite.
exercise: «Ignoring someone who says hello is a discourtesy.» What is a discourtesy in this sentence? | A long journey | A type of weather | *One rude act | A kind surprise party
exercise: Which word is the opposite of discourtesy? | Rudeness | *Courtesy | Discourse | Disorder
exercise: A teacher writes, «Her discourtesy to the visitor was noted.» What does discourtesy mean? | A loud noise | *Rude, impolite behaviour | A tiny gift | Kindness and good manners
test: «It would be a discourtesy to arrive late.» Which phrase means nearly the same? | Being hungry | Being polite | Being early | *Being impolite
test: Which sentence uses discourteous correctly? | The discourteous cake was tasty. | *The discourteous guest did not say thank you. | We went discourteous to the park. | Discourteous is a colour of paint.
exam: «He made an act of discourtesy by pushing in front of the queue.» What is an act of discourtesy? | *A single rude act | Helping someone carry their bags | A rainy day | A kind thank-you note
